---The fallback configuration for a route to an inference target. Defines an ordered list of fallback targets to try when a request to the route's target fails, and the conditions that trigger a fallback. A fallback can occur only before the gateway sends the first byte of the response to the caller. After a streaming response starts, the gateway doesn't fall back.
---@class aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.Fallback
---@field triggerOn? aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.FallbackTriggers The status codes and errors from the route's target that cause the gateway to send the request to the first fallback target. If you omit triggerOn, the gateway falls back on 5XX status codes and on the CONNECTION_ERROR, FIRST_BYTE_TIMEOUT, and UNROUTABLE errors. If you specify triggerOn, only the status codes and errors that you list trigger a fallback.
---@field firstByteTimeoutMilliseconds? number The maximum time, in milliseconds, from sending the request to the route's target until the first byte of the response body arrives. If the time expires, the gateway abandons the request and treats it as a FIRST_BYTE_TIMEOUT error. If you don't specify a value, no timeout is enforced.
---@field circuitBreaker? aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.CircuitBreakerConfiguration Specifies whether the gateway temporarily stops sending your requests to a failing target. The circuit breaker tracks each combination of target and model separately. With the circuit breaker enabled, the gateway skips one or more targets and models that fail repeatedly, and your requests go to the next target in the chain. The gateway always tries the last remaining target in the chain. The gatew...
---@field targetFallback aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.TargetFallbacks The ordered list of fallback targets. The gateway tries each target in order until a response doesn't match that target's triggers, and returns that response to the caller. If every target fails, the gateway returns the last response. You can specify up to two fallback targets. Each combination of target and model, including the route's target, can appear only once.

---@alias aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.FallbackError "CONNECTION_ERROR"|"FIRST_BYTE_TIMEOUT"|"UNROUTABLE"

---@alias aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.FallbackErrors (aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.FallbackError|string)[]

---Specifies a target to send the request to when the previous target in the fallback chain fails. Includes the target name, the model to send, and the conditions that trigger a fallback from this target to the next one.
---@class aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.FallbackTarget
---@field targetName aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.TargetName|distilled.Secret The name of the gateway target to fall back to. The target must be an inference target.
---@field model? aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.ConcreteModelId The model ID to send to this fallback target. If you don't specify a model, the gateway sends the model from the original request.
---@field triggerOn? aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.FallbackTriggers The status codes and errors from this target that cause the gateway to send the request to the next fallback target. This setting isn't inherited from the route. If you omit it, the gateway uses the default triggers: 5XX status codes and the CONNECTION_ERROR, FIRST_BYTE_TIMEOUT, and UNROUTABLE errors.
---@field firstByteTimeoutMilliseconds? number The maximum time, in milliseconds, from sending the request to this target until the first byte of the response body arrives. This setting isn't inherited from the route. If you don't specify a value, no timeout is enforced.

---The conditions that trigger a fallback to the next target. A fallback occurs if the response matches any of the specified status codes or errors.
---@class aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.FallbackTriggers
---@field statusCodes? aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.ErrorStatusCodePatterns The HTTP status codes returned by the target that trigger a fallback. You can specify the following:
---@field errors? aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.FallbackErrors The errors that trigger a fallback. You can specify the following:

