---@field name aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.PolicyName The customer-assigned immutable name for the policy. This human-readable identifier must be unique within the account and cannot exceed 48 characters.
---@field policyEngineId aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.ResourceId The identifier of the policy engine that manages this policy. This establishes the policy engine context for policy evaluation and management.
---@field createdAt aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.DateTimestamp The timestamp when the policy was originally created. This is automatically set by the service and used for auditing and lifecycle management.
---@field updatedAt aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.DateTimestamp The timestamp when the policy was last modified. This tracks the most recent changes to the policy configuration or metadata.
---@field policyArn aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.PolicyArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the policy. This globally unique identifier can be used for cross-service references and IAM policy statements.
---@field status aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.PolicyStatus The current status of the policy.
---@field enforcementMode aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.EnforcementMode The current enforcement mode of the policy.
---@field definition aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.PolicyDefinition The Cedar or Dogwood policy statement that defines the access control rules. This contains the actual policy logic used for agent behavior control and access decisions.
---@field description? distilled.Secret A human-readable description of the policy's purpose and functionality. Limited to 4,096 characters, this helps administrators understand and manage the policy.
---@field statusReasons aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.PolicyStatusReasons Additional information about the policy status. This provides details about any failures or the current state of the policy lifecycle.

---@alias aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.PolicyArn string

---Represents the definition structure for policies within the AgentCore Policy system. This structure encapsulates different policy formats and languages that can be used to define access control rules.
---@class aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.PolicyDefinition
---@field cedar? aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.CedarPolicy The Cedar policy definition within the policy definition structure. This contains the Cedar policy statement that defines the authorization logic using Cedar's human-readable, analyzable policy language. Cedar policies specify principals (who can access), actions (what operations are allowed), resources (what can be accessed), and optional conditions for fine-grained control. Cedar provides a form...
---@field policyGeneration? aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.PolicyGenerationDetails The generated policy asset information within the policy definition structure. This contains information identifying a generated policy asset from the AI-powered policy generation process within the AgentCore Policy system. Each asset contains a Dogwood policy statement generated from natural language input, along with associated metadata and analysis findings to help users evaluate and select the...
---@field policy? aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.PolicyStatement The Dogwood policy statement that defines the access control rules. This policy definition can include Dogwood policies and supports temporal conditions and information providers such as guardrails.

---Represents a policy engine resource within the AgentCore Policy system. Policy engines serve as containers for grouping related policies and provide the execution context for policy evaluation and management. Each policy engine can be associated with one Gateway (one engine per Gateway), where it intercepts all agent tool calls and evaluates them against the contained policies before allowing tool...
---@class aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.PolicyEngine
---@field policyEngineId aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.ResourceId The unique identifier for the policy engine. This system-generated identifier consists of the user name plus a 10-character generated suffix and serves as the primary key for policy engine operations.
---@field name aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.PolicyEngineName The customer-assigned immutable name for the policy engine. This human-readable identifier must be unique within the account and cannot exceed 48 characters.
---@field createdAt aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.DateTimestamp The timestamp when the policy engine was originally created. This is automatically set by the service and used for auditing and lifecycle management.
---@field updatedAt aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.DateTimestamp The timestamp when the policy engine was last modified. This tracks the most recent changes to the policy engine configuration or metadata.
---@field policyEngineArn aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.PolicyEngineArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the policy engine. This globally unique identifier can be used for cross-service references and IAM policy statements.
---@field status aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.PolicyEngineStatus The current status of the policy engine.
---@field encryptionKeyArn? aws.bedrock_agentcore_control.KmsKeyArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the KMS key used to encrypt the policy engine data.
---@field description? distilled.Secret A human-readable description of the policy engine's purpose and scope. Limited to 4,096 characters, this helps administrators understand the policy engine's role in the overall governance strategy.
